🇺🇸🇺🇦🇷🇺US Fully Restores Starlink/Starsheild for Ukraine

▪️ The US says it fully restored access to Starlink/Starsheild for Ukraine, thus concluding this episode of Trump-Zelensky political theater;

▪️Whether the US sought to create plausible deniability or buy time for its war on Russia in Ukraine while prepping for renewed attacks on Iran, or SpaceX simply suffered an embarrassing failure - it is now admittedly restored, once again revealing any sort of serious US-Ukraine "split" as purely performative;

▪️Even during the "shutdown" Ukraine, with US assistance, continued striking Russian energy production/storage facilities deep inside Russian territory while many Ukrainian units reported Starlink/Starsheild services were spotty, not entirely disabled;

▪️I'm often asked why Russia plays along with such theater - it's likely Russia recognizes its own weaknesses and seeks to lend the US plausible deniability and an exit from the conflict in Ukraine if it rapidly deteriorates - allowing the US to simply pretend Ukraine isn't cooperating and claim its collapse is entirely Ukraine's own fault - something along those lines to avoid escalation directly between the US/Russia;

▪️Of course, even if Ukraine collapses, the US is already preparing additional proxies to take its place - the Baltics, even Germany come to mind - maybe Russia is confident it can deal with that as well or will worry about it when it arrives at that juncture;

